
Michael Goldenitz
Aspiring Health and Drug-Safety Data Analyst. I'm in the Applied Data Analytics and Visualization program at Sheridan College (Mississauga) and have an HBSc in Psychology and Philosophy from the University of Toronto Mississauga, with neuroscience coursework and an FSL brain-imaging research project.

My project areas include drug approvals, clinical trials, safety reporting, population harms and hospital emergency departments. They use SQL, Python, R, Power BI and AWS on public Canadian and US health data.

Start here
Mental Health Clinical Trials Pipeline: 18,357 ClinicalTrials.gov trials, SQL, Power BI and a live app, refreshed weekly on AWS. Anxiety trials grew 5.7 times from 2010-12 to 2023-25; Canada ranks second, after the US, with 1,020 trials that have a Canadian site.
Safety Signal Explorer: Adverse event reports for esketamine (Spravato) and ketamine in 10.8 million FAERS cases and 567,733 Canada Vigilance reports. All 8 known reactions used as checks were flagged, and none of the 4 negative controls were.
Ontario ER Wait-Time Scorecard: Power BI scorecard for Trillium Health Partners' three sites against 150+ Ontario EDs. Credit Valley's admitted patients spend 8.3 hours longer in the ED than Mississauga's after adjusting for volume and patient mix.
Also
Canadian Drug Products Database: SQL analysis of 50,960 Health Canada drug products.
Ontario Substance Harms Forecast: Opioid and stimulant deaths and hospitalizations forecast to Q2 2027 in Python, R and Excel.
Brain Changes Across the Lifespan: Pre-registered analysis of 563 MRI scans; brain age predicted within 7.4 years on average.
